<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  DEMO-ONLY visual dress-up of the M2 AprilTag target: same tag, wrapped in a
  primitive-built "enemy FPV quadcopter" body so the portfolio demo video
  reads as "interceptor catches an enemy drone" rather than "interceptor
  catches a printed board". Built for scripts/../worlds/apriltag_demo.sdf;
  the gated worlds (worlds/apriltag.sdf etc.) keep using the plain
  models/apriltag_target board untouched -- no gated number depends on this
  file.

  DETECTION CONTRACT (do not break): the <visual name='tag_visual'> block
  below is copied VERBATIM from models/apriltag_target/model.sdf -- same
  pose (0 0 0 0 -1.5708 0), same plane size (0.625 m/side -> 0.5 m
  pupil-apriltags tag_size per that model's own derivation comment), same
  emissive_map material (ADR-0007 -- emissive is what makes the tag
  decodable at range independent of scene lighting; a flat/albedo-only
  material would silently reintroduce the detection-range regression ADR-0007
  fixed). It resolves the SAME texture file via
  model://apriltag_target/tag36h11_00000.png rather than a duplicated copy,
  so there is exactly one tag image asset in the repo and zero drift risk
  between the two models. If this model is included with the same pose used
  for apriltag_target today (see worlds/apriltag.sdf's `5 0 0.5 0 0 0`), the
  detected tag geometry is byte-identical to the current gated target.

  OCCLUSION SAFETY (why the body can't hide the tag): everything added below
  is either
    (a) behind the tag plane in local +X (the model's local -X is the
        "outward"/approach-facing normal per ADR-0007's derivation, so +X is
        "aft"/away from the approaching interceptor) -- these parts are only
        ever visible where they extend PAST the tag's own 0.625 m square
        footprint (|local Y| or |local Z| > 0.3125), because the opaque tag
        plane at local X=0 sits in front of them and occludes the rest; or
    (b) entirely outside the tag's 0.625 m square footprint in Y/Z (the
        camera/antenna nub, placed above the tag's top edge), so it never
        overlaps the tag's rendered pixels regardless of its X depth.
  See the per-visual comments for the numbers. No collision geometry is
  added (mirrors apriltag_target, which also has none -- ADR-0009 addendum
  notes a flythrough is physically harmless; keeping that true here avoids
  introducing any new physics behavior for a purely cosmetic model).

  BODY RE-ORIENT (portfolio demo polish, builder feedback: the drone read as
  "strafing sideways" instead of "flying forward along its travel path" --
  the hero flight crosses along +Y, worlds/apriltag_demo.sdf --target-vel
  0,9.0). FIX: yaw the fuselage box (body_visual) and the camera/antenna nub
  (cam_nub_visual) -90 deg about LOCAL Z so their elongated/offset axis now
  points along Y instead of X -- these are the only two parts with a
  directional "nose" read. The 4-fold-symmetric arm/prop/hub "shield" ring
  (radially diagonal in the Y-Z plane, no inherent front/back) is left
  COMPLETELY UNCHANGED, on purpose: a naive whole-assembly rotation about
  the tag's own local origin was checked with a small numeric script and
  DOES push the hub/prop/arm centers to local X<0 (in FRONT of the tag
  plane, e.g. hub_ne_visual's center goes from (0.155,-0.354,0.354) to
  (-0.354,-0.155,0.354)) while still inside/near the tag's Y/Z footprint --
  a real occlusion breach. So instead of rotating POSITIONS about the tag's
  origin, only the ORIENTATION (yaw field) of body_visual changes, its
  POSITION stays byte-identical (0.14 0 0) -- since SDF pose composition is
  R = Rz(yaw)*Ry(pitch)*Rx(roll), adding a yaw to an already-yaw=0 pose is
  just "new_yaw = -1.570796", nothing else. This keeps the box fully within
  X in [0.06, 0.22] (still 100% behind/hidden by the tag from the
  interceptor's own -X approach view, exactly as before -- verified by hand:
  the box was ALREADY completely hidden from head-on in the original
  orientation too, since its old Y/Z half-extents (0.08/0.05) sat inside the
  tag's 0.3125 m footprint; this re-orient is a pure no-op for the
  interceptor's onboard camera, and ONLY changes the CHASE-camera's oblique
  broadside read -- so it cannot affect detection). cam_nub_visual is
  REPOSITIONED (not just re-yawed -- its footprint is X/Y-symmetric so a yaw
  alone wouldn't visibly move it) from (-0.03,0,0.36) to (0,0.03,0.36),
  sliding its small "forward offset" from the old nose axis (-X) onto the
  new one (+Y); it stays safe unconditionally because Z=0.36 (+/-0.025 half-
  height) is outside the tag's +/-0.3125 footprint on Z alone, regardless of
  X/Y. Net result: the fuselage's long axis and its little canopy/antenna
  marker both point along the travel direction; the tag itself did not move
  a millimeter (see DETECTION CONTRACT above, still byte-identical).
-->
<sdf version='1.9'>
  <model name='fpv_target'>
    <static>true</static>
    <link name='base'>

      <!-- ================= THE TAG (unchanged -- see header) ================= -->
      <visual name='tag_visual'>
        <pose>0 0 0 0 -1.5708 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <plane>
            <normal>0 0 1</normal>
            <size>0.625 0.625</size>
          </plane>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0 0 0 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0 0 0 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0 0 0 1</specular>
          <pbr>
            <metal>
              <albedo_map>model://apriltag_target/tag36h11_00000.png</albedo_map>
              <emissive_map>model://apriltag_target/tag36h11_00000.png</emissive_map>
              <roughness>1.0</roughness>
              <metalness>0.0</metalness>
            </metal>
          </pbr>
        </material>
      </visual>

      <!-- ================= ENEMY QUAD BODY (decoration only) =================
           Local frame recap: -X = front/outward (tag-facing side, toward the
           approaching interceptor), +X = aft. Y = left/right, Z = up/down
           (matches the tag's own span so "beyond the tag's edge" means
           |Y|>0.3125 or |Z|>0.3125). Everything below is dark carbon
           (near-black) with a few red "enemy" accents. -->

      <!-- Central fuselage: fully behind the tag (X in [0.06,0.22] after the
           yaw below -- still inside [0.04,0.24]) and smaller than the tag's
           0.3125 m half-width/half-height in Y/Z, so it is completely
           hidden behind the opaque tag plane from a -X (approach) view --
           it only matters for oblique/side demo angles. Position
           UNCHANGED; yaw=-90deg (see header "BODY RE-ORIENT") swaps the
           box's long 0.20 m axis from local X onto local Y, so it reads as
           pointing along the target's +Y travel direction instead of the
           old approach-facing X axis. -->
      <visual name='body_visual'>
        <pose>0.14 0 0 0 0 -1.570796</pose>
        <geometry>
          <box>
            <size>0.20 0.16 0.10</size>
          </box>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.03 0.03 0.035 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.05 0.05 0.06 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.25 0.25 0.28 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>

      <!-- 4 arms, X-quad layout, built as cylinders rolled about the local
           X axis (roll only -> every point on each cylinder stays at
           local X = 0.14 +/- radius, i.e. strictly behind the tag plane at
           X=0; roll just fans the length direction out into the Y-Z plane).
           roll = 45/135/225/315 deg picks the 4 diagonal quadrants; radial
           midpoint 0.29 m, length 0.42 m -> tips reach radial 0.50 m, i.e.
           |Y|=|Z|=0.354 m at the diagonal, past the tag's 0.3125 m half-
           width/height, so the outer ~40% of each arm peeks past the tag's
           corners (the "this is mounted on a drone" read) while the inner
           run is hidden behind the tag. -->
      <visual name='arm_ne_visual'>
        <pose>0.14 -0.205061 0.205061 0.785398 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder>
            <radius>0.013</radius>
            <length>0.42</length>
          </cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.03 0.03 0.035 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.05 0.05 0.06 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.25 0.25 0.28 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <visual name='arm_se_visual'>
        <pose>0.14 -0.205061 -0.205061 2.356194 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder>
            <radius>0.013</radius>
            <length>0.42</length>
          </cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.03 0.03 0.035 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.05 0.05 0.06 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.25 0.25 0.28 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <visual name='arm_sw_visual'>
        <pose>0.14 0.205061 -0.205061 3.926991 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder>
            <radius>0.013</radius>
            <length>0.42</length>
          </cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.03 0.03 0.035 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.05 0.05 0.06 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.25 0.25 0.28 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <visual name='arm_nw_visual'>
        <pose>0.14 0.205061 0.205061 5.497787 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder>
            <radius>0.013</radius>
            <length>0.42</length>
          </cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.03 0.03 0.035 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.05 0.05 0.06 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.25 0.25 0.28 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>

      <!-- 4 prop discs: thin cylinders pitched +90 deg about local Y so
           their length axis (thickness, 6 mm) runs along local X and their
           radius (95 mm) fans out in the Y-Z plane -- i.e. a flat disc
           facing the camera, like a propeller viewed near head-on. Centered
           at the same radial-0.50 m diagonal points as the arm tips, depth
           X=0.17 (still behind the tag at X=0). Semi-transparent to read as
           a spinning blur rather than a solid can. -->
      <visual name='prop_ne_visual'>
        <pose>0.17 -0.353553 0.353553 0 1.570796 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder>
            <radius>0.095</radius>
            <length>0.006</length>
          </cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <transparency>0.5</transparency>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.15 0.15 0.16 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.18 0.18 0.19 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.3 0.3 0.3 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <visual name='prop_se_visual'>
        <pose>0.17 -0.353553 -0.353553 0 1.570796 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder>
            <radius>0.095</radius>
            <length>0.006</length>
          </cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <transparency>0.5</transparency>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.15 0.15 0.16 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.18 0.18 0.19 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.3 0.3 0.3 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <visual name='prop_sw_visual'>
        <pose>0.17 0.353553 -0.353553 0 1.570796 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder>
            <radius>0.095</radius>
            <length>0.006</length>
          </cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <transparency>0.5</transparency>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.15 0.15 0.16 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.18 0.18 0.19 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.3 0.3 0.3 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <visual name='prop_nw_visual'>
        <pose>0.17 0.353553 0.353553 0 1.570796 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder>
            <radius>0.095</radius>
            <length>0.006</length>
          </cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <transparency>0.5</transparency>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.15 0.15 0.16 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.18 0.18 0.19 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.3 0.3 0.3 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>

      <!-- 4 motor hubs, same diagonal positions as the prop discs (depth
           X=0.155, between the arm plane and the prop-disc plane), small
           pitched cylinders. Diagonal pair NE/SW painted red as an "enemy"
           strobe/ID accent; the other diagonal pair (SE/NW) stays dark
           carbon like the rest of the airframe. -->
      <visual name='hub_ne_visual'>
        <pose>0.155 -0.353553 0.353553 0 1.570796 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder>
            <radius>0.022</radius>
            <length>0.03</length>
          </cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.25 0.02 0.02 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.65 0.05 0.05 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.3 0.1 0.1 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <visual name='hub_se_visual'>
        <pose>0.155 -0.353553 -0.353553 0 1.570796 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder>
            <radius>0.022</radius>
            <length>0.03</length>
          </cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.03 0.03 0.035 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.05 0.05 0.06 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.25 0.25 0.28 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <visual name='hub_sw_visual'>
        <pose>0.155 0.353553 -0.353553 0 1.570796 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder>
            <radius>0.022</radius>
            <length>0.03</length>
          </cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.25 0.02 0.02 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.65 0.05 0.05 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.3 0.1 0.1 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <visual name='hub_nw_visual'>
        <pose>0.155 0.353553 0.353553 0 1.570796 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder>
            <radius>0.022</radius>
            <length>0.03</length>
          </cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.03 0.03 0.035 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.05 0.05 0.06 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.25 0.25 0.28 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>

      <!-- Small camera/antenna nub, red. Positioned ABOVE the tag's top
           edge (local Z=0.36 > the tag's 0.3125 m half-height, so its
           whole 0.025 m half-height still clears 0.335 > 0.3125) -- i.e. it
           never overlaps the tag's Y/Z footprint at all REGARDLESS of its
           X/Y position, so it is safe to slide its small forward offset
           from the old nose axis (local X=-0.03, toward the camera) onto
           the new one (local Y=+0.03, "BODY RE-ORIENT" above) without ever
           occluding a tag pixel. Reads as an FPV cam pod / antenna peeking
           over the top of the tag "shield", now offset toward the travel
           direction instead of the approach direction. -->
      <visual name='cam_nub_visual'>
        <pose>0 0.03 0.36 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <box>
            <size>0.04 0.04 0.05</size>
          </box>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.25 0.02 0.02 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.65 0.05 0.05 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.3 0.1 0.1 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>

    </link>
  </model>
</sdf>
